WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.281
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book three.

2
00:00:05.581 --> 00:00:08.851
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.151 --> 00:00:15.832
Unit twenty-one: Migration and Identity. Today you will mix past and present with mixed conditionals.

4
00:00:16.132 --> 00:00:18.749
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:23.014
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:25.002
Migration.

7
00:00:26.017 --> 00:00:28.794
Migration means moving to live in another place.

8
00:00:29.383 --> 00:00:31.638
Migration to cities is increasing.

9
00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:35.007
Your turn. Say: Migration.

10
00:00:37.867 --> 00:00:38.984
Migration.

11
00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:40.565
Migrant.

12
00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:44.502
Migrant means a person who moves to live somewhere else.

13
00:00:45.117 --> 00:00:46.896
Many migrants work in Thailand.

14
00:00:47.483 --> 00:00:50.159
Your turn. Say: Migrant.

15
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:53.862
Migrant.

16
00:00:54.617 --> 00:00:55.792
Identity.

17
00:00:56.783 --> 00:00:58.481
Identity means who you are.

18
00:00:59.083 --> 00:01:00.955
Language is part of identity.

19
00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:04.260
Your turn. Say: Identity.

20
00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.171
Identity.

21
00:01:08.917 --> 00:01:09.883
Culture.

22
00:01:10.883 --> 00:01:13.463
Culture means the customs and beliefs of a group.

23
00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:16.212
She keeps her culture alive abroad.

24
00:01:16.817 --> 00:01:19.237
Your turn. Say: Culture.

25
00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:22.997
Culture.

26
00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:24.948
Integration.

27
00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:28.809
Integration means becoming part of a new community.

28
00:01:29.417 --> 00:01:31.590
Language classes help integration.

29
00:01:32.183 --> 00:01:35.172
Your turn. Say: Integration.

30
00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:39.139
Integration.

31
00:01:39.883 --> 00:01:40.617
Home.

32
00:01:41.617 --> 00:01:43.628
Home means the place where you belong.

33
00:01:44.217 --> 00:01:46.089
Home is where my family is.

34
00:01:46.683 --> 00:01:48.639
Your turn. Say: Home.

35
00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:52.443
Home.

36
00:01:53.183 --> 00:01:54.405
Opportunity.

37
00:01:55.417 --> 00:01:58.020
Opportunity means a chance for something better.

38
00:01:58.617 --> 00:02:00.605
Migrants look for opportunity.

39
00:02:01.217 --> 00:02:04.055
Your turn. Say: Opportunity.

40
00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:08.087
Opportunity.

41
00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:09.828
Belonging.

42
00:02:10.817 --> 00:02:13.002
Belonging means feeling part of a group.

43
00:02:13.617 --> 00:02:15.570
A sense of belonging is important.

44
00:02:16.183 --> 00:02:18.696
Your turn. Say: Belonging.

45
00:02:21.533 --> 00:02:22.616
Belonging.

46
00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:26.842
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:27.683 --> 00:02:30.020
Visal, have you thought about living abroad?

48
00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:36.079
Yes. If I had moved abroad, I would speak another language now.

49
00:02:37.183 --> 00:02:38.463
What would be hard?

50
00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:44.791
If my uncle hadn't left Cambodia, he would be with us now. He misses home.

51
00:02:45.883 --> 00:02:47.198
And his identity?

52
00:02:48.283 --> 00:02:53.513
He feels both Khmer and Australian. He has found belonging in two places.

53
00:02:54.667 --> 00:02:56.295
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:59.939
Grammar focus: Mixed conditionals.

55
00:03:00.239 --> 00:03:01.507
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:02.217 --> 00:03:05.482
If I had moved abroad, I would speak another language now.

57
00:03:06.383 --> 00:03:08.743
If he hadn't left, he would be with us today.

58
00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:13.530
If she had learned English earlier, she would have a better job now.

59
00:03:14.467 --> 00:03:20.797
A mixed conditional links a past condition to a present result: If + past perfect, would + base verb.

60
00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:26.350
Be careful! Don't say: If I had moved abroad, I would spoke another language now.

61
00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:32.250
Say: If I had moved abroad, I would speak another language now.

62
00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:34.422
After 'would', use the base verb.

63
00:03:35.233 --> 00:03:37.781
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:38.567 --> 00:03:39.939
Between Two Homes.

65
00:03:40.239 --> 00:03:42.529
Migration changes millions of lives.

66
00:03:43.533 --> 00:03:46.531
Migrants look for opportunity but often miss home.

67
00:03:47.533 --> 00:03:50.868
Integration takes time, language and kindness.

68
00:03:51.867 --> 00:03:55.178
If my uncle hadn't moved, he wouldn't have two cultures now.

69
00:03:56.167 --> 00:03:59.339
Identity and belonging can grow in more than one place.

70
00:04:00.433 --> 00:04:04.783
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:08.195
If I had moved, I blank speak French now.

72
00:04:08.495 --> 00:04:11.475
A, would. B, will. C, had.

73
00:04:15.033 --> 00:04:16.777
The answer is A: would.

74
00:04:17.917 --> 00:04:20.485
Becoming part of a new community is blank.

75
00:04:20.785 --> 00:04:25.065
A, integration. B, migration. C, identity.

76
00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:31.215
The answer is A: integration.

77
00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:34.361
Feeling part of a group is blank.

78
00:04:34.661 --> 00:04:38.616
A, belonging. B, culture. C, opportunity.

79
00:04:42.167 --> 00:04:44.155
The answer is A: belonging.

80
00:04:45.367 --> 00:04:48.588
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:51.624
What challenges might migrants face?

82
00:05:00.417 --> 00:05:01.812
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:05:02.112 --> 00:05:12.648
Migrants might face language problems and loneliness. If my aunt had learned Korean before she moved, she would feel more at home now.

84
00:05:12.948 --> 00:05:14.599
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:15.483 --> 00:05:19.529
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and mixed conditionals.

86
00:05:19.829 --> 00:05:23.282
Today's value is empathy. Think about how others feel.

87
00:05:23.582 --> 00:05:26.328
See you in Unit twenty-two. Goodbye!

88
00:05:26.628 --> 00:05:29.756
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

